@startuml
title Follow Route / Trajectory MVP Sequence

skinparam shadowing false

actor Operator
participant TacticalGraphicsEditorController as RouteUI
participant GraphicPickCoordinator as Picker
participant ScenarioState
participant AssignTaskDialog
participant TaskApplicator
participant RouteTask
participant FlightDynamicsEngine as FDE
participant EntityPlanExecutor as PlanExec

Operator -> RouteUI: create/edit route
RouteUI -> Picker: beginRoutePick(name, default altitude)

loop each route point
  Operator -> Picker: click map coordinate
  alt Air route
    Picker -> Operator: prompt altitudeMeters
    Operator --> Picker: altitudeMeters
  else Ground route
    Picker -> Picker: altitudeMeters = 0
  end
  Picker -> ScenarioState: add/update RouteGraphic(RoutePoint lat/lon/alt)
end

Operator -> AssignTaskDialog: Task > Movement > Follow Route
AssignTaskDialog --> TaskApplicator: EntityTask(FollowRoute, targetRouteName, tolerance, timeout)
TaskApplicator -> ScenarioState: lookup route points
TaskApplicator -> RouteTask: create(points, speed, arrivalTolerance)

loop simulation ticks
  FDE -> RouteTask: evaluate(entity position)

  alt current waypoint reached
    RouteTask -> RouteTask: distance <= arrivalTolerance
    RouteTask -> RouteTask: advance to next waypoint
  else safe overshoot
    RouteTask -> RouteTask: was close, now distance grows
    RouteTask -> RouteTask: mark waypoint reached
  else still en route
    RouteTask --> FDE: heading to current waypoint, waypoint altitude, speed
  end

  alt last waypoint completed
    RouteTask --> FDE: State Completed
    FDE -> ScenarioState: currentTask.status = Completed
    PlanExec -> PlanExec: mark step Completed
    PlanExec -> TaskApplicator: start next step
  else timeout
    FDE -> ScenarioState: currentTask.status = Failed
  end
end

note right of RouteTask
Overshoot is not failure.
It only advances if the entity
was close enough to the waypoint.

This prevents skipping far waypoints.
end note

note right of TaskApplicator
Altitude rules:
- Air: route point altitude if set
- Air legacy missing altitude: current/previous altitude
- Ground: 0 m
end note

@enduml
